<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net6.0;net7.0;net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <RootNamespace>Kebechet.Blazor.Swiper</RootNamespace>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Label="NugetProperties">
    <Authors>Kebechet</Authors>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>Kebechet.Blazor.Swiper</PackageId>
    <Description>Blazor wrapper for the Swiper touch slider, built on the framework-agnostic Swiper Element web component. Ships the Swiper bundle and auto-registers it - no npm or manual script tags.</Description>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Kebechet/Blazor.Swiper</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Kebechet/Blazor.Swiper</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageTags>blazor;swiper;carousel;slider;slideshow;touch;swipe;webcomponent</PackageTags>
    <!-- First three parts track the bundled Swiper release; the fourth is this wrapper's own revision. -->
    <Version>14.0.6.2</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>BREAKING, and a much larger API. SwiperOptions now mirrors every one of Swiper's parameters - all 95 top-level ones plus the 22 nested module option records - and every member is nullable, so an unset member is the only signal for "keep Swiper's default". All 77 of Swiper's events now have a callback, subscribed only when you assign one, so an unwired event costs no listener and no interop. ActiveIndex is two-way bindable (@bind-ActiveIndex), as is IsAutoplayRunning. Options is now reactive: changing it pushes the members that moved to the live slider. Adds GetStateAsync, the full navigation and update method set, Autoplay/Zoom/Keyboard/Mousewheel/Slides/Virtual controllers, Thumbs and Controller cross-instance wiring, slide-level Zoom/Lazy/Hash/AutoplayDelay/VirtualIndex, per-slide state through SlideContent, declarative pagination templates, and EventThrottle for the events that fire per animation frame. Breaking: Direction is now the SwiperDirection enum (SwiperDirection.Horizontal still compiles, a literal "horizontal" does not); Pagination/Navigation/Scrollbar/Keyboard/Mousewheel are option records with an implicit conversion from bool, so `= true` still compiles; previously non-nullable options are nullable; SwiperSlide.ChildContent stays plain and per-slide state moved to SlideContent; the per-event JSInvokable methods collapsed into one dispatcher. Same vendored Swiper 14.0.6 bundle.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <DeterministicSourcePaths Condition="'$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true'">true</DeterministicSourcePaths>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Blazor.Swiper.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net6.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="6.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net7.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="7.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="8.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net9.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="9.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="10.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\..\icon.png">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
